            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-amber-400 mb-4">Complete Beginner's Guide to DMM Flipping (2026)</h1>
            <p class="text-gray-400">Updated: February 2026 • 8 min read</p>
        </header>

        <div class="osrs-card p-8 rounded-lg mb-10">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                Deadman Mode (DMM) is the most volatile and profitable market in Old School RuneScape. Prices can triple in hours or crash in minutes. 
                This guide will teach you how to profit from this chaos using the Grand Exchange and safe deposit boxes.
            </p>
        </div>

        <h2>Why Flip in Deadman Mode?</h2>
        <p>
            Unlike the main game, DMM has a condensed economy. Gear is constantly lost on death, creating perpetual demand. 
            Supplies like Sharks, Brews, and Restores are consumed at massive rates during breaches and finals. 
            This high turnover means <strong>margins are significantly wider</strong> than in regular OSRS.
        </p>

        <h2>1. The Safety First Rule</h2>
        <p>
            In DMM, your bank can be raided if you die. However, the Grand Exchange (GE) offers a unique safety mechanism. 
            <strong>Items currently in GE offers are safe from bank keys.</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Always keep your cash stack invested in high-volume items in the GE when leaving safe zones.</li>
            <li>Use the "Deposit Box" to protect your guaranteed item slots (10 items).</li>
            <li>Never flip with your entire stack if you plan to go PK request; keep liquidity in protected items.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Identifying Profitable Items</h2>
        <p>
            The best items to flip fall into three categories:
        </p>
        
        <h3>Consumables (High Volume)</h3>
        <p>
            Food and potions are safest. Sharks, Karambwans, Saradomin Brews, and Super Restores are always in demand. 
            Margins are smaller (100-500gp) but volume is huge.
        </p>

        <h3>PK Gear (Medium Risk)</h3>
        <p>
            Mystic sets, Black D'hide, Rune Crossbows, and Dragon Daggers. 
            These items are lost frequently. Buy them when active PK times are low (morning EST) and sell during peak hours (evening EST/EU).
        </p>

        <h3>Swap Rates (High Risk/Reward)</h3>
        <p>
            Swapping DMM gold for 07 gold is the endgame for many. 
            Tracking the swap rate is crucial. If the rate is dropping efficiently (e.g., 1:10 to 1:8), it means DMM gold is becoming less valuable relative to 07, so item prices in DMM will likely <em>rise</em> (inflation).
            Use our <a href="/#swap-rates" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">Live Swap Rates</a> table to time your exits.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Finding the Margin</h2>
        <p>
            To find the current margin:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-300 mb-6">
            <li>Buy 1 of the item instantly (Insta-buy price).</li>
            <li>Sell that item instantly (Insta-sell price).</li>
            <li>The difference is your margin.</li>
            <li>Place a buy offer slightly above the insta-sell price.</li>
            <li>Place a sell offer slightly below the insta-buy price.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="bg-gray-800 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-6">
            <p class="font-bold text-amber-400 mb-2">Pro Tip:</p>
            <p>Use the <a href="https://osrsdmmge.online" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">osrsdmmge.online</a> real-time price tracker to see margins without spending gold on margin checks.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>4. When to Hold (Investing)</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Breach Investing:</strong> Prices for gear and supplies skyrocket 1-2 hours before a major Breach event. 
            Buy supplies 10 hours before a breach and sell them 30 minutes before it starts.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Avoiding "Crashers"</h2>
        <p>
            DMM economies move fast. If an item isn't buying after 15 minutes, re-check the price. 
            Don't leave offers in overnight unless you are targeting very low ball offers on expensive gear like Ancient Warrior weapons.
        </p>

